         (1.483-1.531) at all 25 wavelength points: TIR verified (plan R16).
           TIR critical angle for PS/FluoPoly:   arcsin(1.42/1.59) = 63.4 deg
           TIR critical angle for PMMA/FluoPoly: arcsin(1.42/1.49) = 72.6 deg
         No ABSLENGTH defined in source (DRsimMaterials.cc section 3.8 note).
         Photons escaping the core into cladding travel unattenuated; in Geant4
         they experience TIR at the core/clad boundary for the appropriate angles.
    -->
    <material name="DR_FluorinatedPolymer">
      <!-- Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:73-138 -->
      <D type="density" value="1.43" unit="g/cm3"/>
      <composite n="2" ref="C"/>
      <composite n="2" ref="F"/>
      <property name="RINDEX" ref="RINDEX__DR_FluorinatedPolymer"/>
      <!-- No ABSLENGTH: source defines none for cladding (see section 3.8 note).
           Photons in cladding travel with zero attenuation. -->
    </material>

    <!-- DR_LightguideMedium: lightguide or cookie material
         Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:77-79 (composition) and 170-175 (optical).

         Q7 RESOLUTION: Source named this material "Glass" (DRsimMaterials.cc:77).
         Actual composition: 91.533 % C + 8.467 % H by mass, density 1.032 g/cm3.
         This is a hydrocarbon, NOT silicate glass (no Si, no O).
         The source name "Glass" is misleading and a collision risk with real
         glass materials (e.g. silicate) in the epic tree (plan R3, R7).
         Based on RINDEX=1.52 and ABSLENGTH=420 cm this matches a clear lightguide
         or optical-cookie medium.  Renamed to DR_LightguideMedium.

         NOTE: Not used in the default DR_Prototype geometry.
         Defined here for completeness of the port and potential future use
         if lightguide volumes are added between fiber ends and SiPMs.
    -->
    <!-- UNUSED in default DR prototype geometry. Ported from source palette for future variants (lightguide/cookie coupling between fiber end and SiPM). Do not include placement in plugin. -->
    <material name="DR_LightguideMedium">
      <!-- Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:77-175.
           Source name "Glass" renamed to DR_LightguideMedium; see Q7 in header. -->
      <D type="density" value="1.032" unit="g/cm3"/>
      <!-- Mass fractions from source: 91.533% C + 8.467% H -->
      <fraction n="0.91533" ref="C"/>
      <fraction n="0.08467" ref="H"/>
      <property name="RINDEX"    ref="RINDEX__DR_LightguideMedium"/>
      <property name="ABSLENGTH" ref="ABSLENGTH__DR_LightguideMedium"/>
    </material>

    <!-- DR_FilterBody: Gelatin substrate for the long-pass optical filter
         Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:90-94 (composition) and 195-198 (optical).
         Composition: C102H151N31O39 (photographic filter dye substrate), density 1.27 g/cm3.
         RINDEX = 1.52 flat (from RI_gel[25] in source, applied to fGelatin).
         The filter surface transmittance properties are on DR_FilterSurf (see surfaces below).

         NOT bound to any volume in the default DR_Prototype geometry (plan decision 10, Q9).
         Available as a Phase 3 diagnostic if C-channel yield overshoots target.
    -->
    <!-- UNUSED in default DR prototype geometry. Ported from source palette for future optical-filter diagnostic. Do not include placement in plugin. -->
    <material name="DR_FilterBody">
      <!-- Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:90-198 -->
      <D type="density" value="1.27" unit="g/cm3"/>
      <composite n="102" ref="C"/>
      <composite n="151" ref="H"/>
      <composite n="31"  ref="N"/>
      <composite n="39"  ref="O"/>
      <property name="RINDEX" ref="RINDEX__DR_FilterBody"/>
    </material>

    <!--
      DR_Air: SiPM window ambient medium.

      DR_Air is ALIASED to AirOptical, which is already defined in
      epic/compact/optical_materials.xml:999-1006.
      AirOptical properties:
        RINDEX    = 1.00029 (flat, 1.0-5.1 eV range) satisfies plan "RINDEX ~= 1.0"
        ABSLENGTH = 4.0 cm (flat)
      Composition: N(75.4%) + O(23.4%) + Ar(1.2%), density 0.0012 g/cm3.

      Source: DRsimMaterials.cc:115-118 defines G4_AIR RINDEX = 1.0 flat (25 points);
      our AirOptical is equivalent (1.00029 rounds to 1.0 at all relevant wavelengths).

      Without RINDEX on the SiPM-window medium, G4OpBoundaryProcess emits NoRINDEX
      warnings and photon boundary status is undefined (plan round-3 change 1a, R16).

      Plugin implementation (P2-beta, todo 2b): use material name "AirOptical" for
      the SiPM window volume.  No separate DR_Air material element is needed here.
      If optical_materials.xml is ever reorganised and AirOptical removed, add:
        <material name="DR_Air">
          <D type="density" unit="g/cm3" value="0.0012"/>
          <fraction n="0.754" ref="N"/>
          <fraction n="0.234" ref="O"/>
          <fraction n="0.012" ref="Ar"/>
          <property name="RINDEX" coldim="2" values="1.0*eV 1.00029  5.1*eV 1.00029"/>
        </material>
    -->

  </materials>

  <!--
    Optical surface definitions.
    All prefixed DR_ to avoid name clashes.
    Syntax follows epic/compact/optical_materials.xml:1165-1207 (dRICH surfaces).
  -->
  <surfaces>

    <!-- DR_SiPMSurf: Hamamatsu S13615-1025N MPPC photosensitive surface
         Final working configuration (confirmed 2026-07-28):
           type = dielectric_dielectric, model = glisur, finish = polished
           EFFICIENCY = 1.0 flat (all photons crossing the boundary are recorded)
         PDE is NOT applied at sim time. Apply at reconstruction:
           lambda [nm] = 2 * pi * hbarc [GeV*nm] / |p [GeV]|
           hbarc = 0.197327e-6 GeV*nm
           PDE(lambda) = np.interp(lambda, pde_lambda[::-1], pde_values[::-1])
           where pde_lambda and pde_values are the EFFICIENCY__DR_SiPMSurf table.
         Why dielectric_dielectric:
           dielectric_metal: REFLECTIVITY table is read, but absorbed photons are
           killed at the boundary before Geant4OpticalTrackerAction fires -> zero hits.
           dielectric_dielectric: photon crosses into the sensitive volume, tracker
           action fires on the step inside -> hit scored. EFFICIENCY table is ignored
           (Fresnel transmission bypasses the roulette), but all photons are recorded
           and wavelength is recoverable from hit momentum.
         Verified tests (2026-07-28, same container, seed 12345, 1 muon 5 GeV):
           dielectric_dielectric + EFFICIENCY=1  -> 1337 hits (baseline)
           dielectric_metal + R=0.0 flat         ->    0 hits (absorbed, not scored)
           dielectric_metal + R=1.0 flat         -> 1288 hits (reflected back, wrongly scored)
           dielectric_metal + R=0.5 flat 25-pt   ->  655 hits (~50% reflected, wrongly scored)
           lambda range from hit momentum: 301-900 nm, mean 547 nm (correct Cherenkov range)
    -->
    <opticalsurface name="DR_SiPMSurf" model="glisur" finish="polished" type="dielectric_dielectric">
      <property name="EFFICIENCY" coldim="2" values="1*eV 1.0  7*eV 1.0"/>
    </opticalsurface>

    <!-- DR_MirrorSurf: generic 90% mirror for fiber far-end reflective caps
         Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:205-212 (fMirrorSurf).
         type = dielectric_metal (source line 211).
         REFLECTIVITY = 0.9 flat, TRANSMITTANCE = 0.0 flat.
         NOT bound to any volume in the default geometry.
         Available for future use if reflective fiber end-caps are added.
    -->
    <!-- UNUSED in default DR prototype geometry (dual-ended readout, no mirrored fiber end). Ported for future single-ended-readout variant. Do not bind in plugin. -->
    <opticalsurface name="DR_MirrorSurf" model="glisur" finish="polished" type="dielectric_metal">
      <property name="REFLECTIVITY" ref="REFLECTIVITY__DR_MirrorSurf"/>
      <property name="TRANSMITTANCE" ref="TRANSMITTANCE__DR_MirrorSurf"/>
    </opticalsurface>

    <!-- DR_FilterSurf: long-pass yellow filter surface
         Ported from DRsimMaterials.cc:189-203 (fFilterSurf).
         type = dielectric_dielectric (source line 202).
         Passes lambda > ~500 nm, blocks below ~420 nm.

         DR_FilterSurf defined but not bound.  Bind as diagnostic only if
         Phase 3 C-channel yield overshoots target.
         (plan-dr-prototype.md section 2a, decision 10 / Q9)
    -->
    <opticalsurface name="DR_FilterSurf" model="glisur" finish="polished" type="dielectric_dielectric">
      <property name="TRANSMITTANCE" ref="TRANSMITTANCE__DR_FilterSurf"/>
      <property name="REFLECTIVITY"  ref="REFLECTIVITY__DR_FilterSurf"/>
    </opticalsurface>

  </surfaces>

</lccdd>
